The regression test is a real discriminator, not a smoke test. It makes the
write itself fail with RLIMIT_FSIZE 0 in a child process (SIGXFSZ ignored, so
the failure is an errno rather than a dead process) and then looks at what is
left -- which is the only way to tell the fix from the bug, since both leave a
file behind. Verified in both directions: against the unfixed lib, 4 of 10
subtests fail (9 assertions: encrypt_file loses the plaintext, rotate loses
the document AND it no longer decrypts, decrypt_file loses the pre-existing
output, all three report success while doing it, plus the inode/hard-link
claim). Against the fixed lib all 10 pass. It skips itself, loudly, if the
harness will not apply the limit.

